       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release, so this is double the limit or more. The risks include lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nIs 1700 mg a typo? These options would fit within the label:\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily**, if you're starting or titrating. The usual start is 500 mg once or twice daily, increased gradually.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If you meant 1,700 mg as the total daily dose, I can enter that as 850 mg twice daily."
